nak: keep the message of a panic caught by nak_compile_shader (GL build only, diagnostics).

nak_compile_shader catches its own panics and returns NULL; the message is only printed
to stderr by the default panic hook, which Android services (SurfaceFlinger) send to
/dev/null. A chained hook (installed once, the previous hook still runs) records the
message with its location per thread; nak_compile_shader_panic_message() returns it so
the gallium driver nvrm can log it through mesa_log (logcat). No change to compilation.

